WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.110
That cheeky devil Lucifer is back and he's
having one hell of a time on Netflix!

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:09.430
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm going to reveal some devilish details

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:14.639
about season 4 of Lucifer including cool easter
eggs, ingenious foreshadowing, secret cameos,

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:16.020
and more things you may have missed.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.210
Obviously, spoilers ahead if you're not all
caught up.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:23.390
If you were shocked by the season 4 finale
where Lucifer confessed his love to Chloe

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.880
and then banished himself from Earth to sit
on the throne in Hell, then you'll be even

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.929
more surprised to know that moment was cleverly
foreshadowed right in the opening scene of

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:32.929
the season.

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:37.730
The premiere episode begins with a montage
of a lonely, melancholy Lucifer singing Radiohead's

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.480
"Creep" at his club Lux.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.260
Chloe's absence and the throne-like art-deco
background behind Luci predicts how he will

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:49.440
end the season: alone again without Chloe,
sitting on a throne overlooking Hell.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.100
The reflection of Lucifer in the piano also
foreshadows how split he'll feel this season

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.720
between his more and less devilish sides and
also how he'll travel from the Earth above

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.170
to the Underworld below.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:05.269
And, in a really clever detail, as the opening
montage plays out, Lucifer's clothes change

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:09.439
with each new day, finishing with him in a
white shirt and dark suit with a little red

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:11.530
handkerchief in his breast pocket.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:15.909
And that's basically the same outfit complete
with red pocket square that we see him wearing

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.880
at the very end of the season when he's sat
on his throne in Hell.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.119
When Chloe visits Father Kinley he shows her
a scrapbook of some of the problems he says

00:01:24.119 --> 00:01:26.750
were caused by Lucifer's previous visits to
earth.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.479
"Once we uncovered Lucifer's identity, we
were able to uncover evidence of his previous

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:32.569
visits with humanity.

00:01:32.569 --> 00:01:33.569
You're...

00:01:33.569 --> 00:01:37.930
You're saying he caused the Chicago Fire and
Nazi Germany?"

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:42.009
And when the detective turns to the page of
clippings from Nazi Germany, there's a photo

00:01:42.009 --> 00:01:44.429
with none other than Lucifer standing there.

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:48.729
However, the devil does not look impressed
with the people he encountered and, I think,

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:52.990
what Father Kinley has misunderstood is that
Lucifer's very likely there to find out all

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.520
about the humans he'll be punishing later
in Hell.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.359
In fact, this links back to previous mentions
of Hitler on the show:

00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:02.299
"How did you actually torture Hitler in Hell?"

00:02:02.299 --> 00:02:03.299
"Hitler was a talker.

00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:04.299
Well, screamer, actually."

00:02:04.299 --> 00:02:07.840
"Shouldn't you be, uh, I don't know, having
tea with Hitler by now?"

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.890
As for the Chicago Fire, well that's a cool
easter egg to one of actress Lauren German's

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.629
previous TV roles.

00:02:13.629 --> 00:02:18.879
The Great Chicago Fire was a real fire that
raged for several days in late 1871, but of

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:22.550
all the historical events that the Lucifer
writers could have picked, they chose this

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:27.790
one as Lauren German, aka Chloe, starred in
two seasons of the TV drama Chicago Fire where

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:29.629
she played a paramedic!

00:02:29.629 --> 00:02:33.790
And it's tricky to make out, but there is
a "Lucifer Morningstar" listed on the check-in

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.480
page for the hotel in Chicago.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.380
When Fox cancelled Lucifer after its third
season, Lucifans responded with a resounding

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.701
'hell, no' and got straight to work online,
letting everyone know just how much the show

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:46.701
meant to them.

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:51.269
Thanks to their online campaign, we got our
deepest desire: a fiendishly good new season

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:52.269
on Netflix.

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:56.250
And there's a sly wink to the show's former
fate, when Father Kinley hands Lucifer his

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:57.299
business card.

00:02:57.299 --> 00:02:58.299
"Vatican investigator?

00:02:58.299 --> 00:03:01.239
Sounds like a soon-to-be-canceled TV show."

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:05.120
And in a grateful shout-out to those many
fans who helped raise the series from the

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.969
dead, the show's writers titled episode 9,
"Save Lucifer", which is a lovely hat-tip

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:13.030
to the hashtag Lucifans used to blow up twitter!

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:18.720
There's a particularly touching moment mid-way
through Season 4 where Amenadiel tells Chloe

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.900
just how proud her father is of her, and the
way he says it shows that he's seen or spoken

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.170
to her father in heaven.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:29.720
After all that you've been through, Chloe...
what you're worried about most is what's best

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.480
for those that you care about.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.900
No wonder your dad is so proud of you."

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:37.989
That revelation is actually a moving reminder
of some of the final words Chloe's police

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:40.320
officer dad said, just before he was murdered.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.299
"Just tell her it was a good movie.

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:43.450
Kids these days.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.709
Yeah, I know.

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:45.709
But, hey...

00:03:45.709 --> 00:03:47.239
I'm proud of her."

00:03:47.239 --> 00:03:51.930
By the way, the actor who played Chloe's father
in those flashbacks in season 2 is Chris Payne

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.769
Gilbert, the real-life husband of Lesley-Ann
Brandt who plays Maze.

00:03:55.769 --> 00:04:00.209
Speaking of Maze, she gets some hilarious
scenes as always in Season 4, but there was

00:04:00.209 --> 00:04:04.319
one particularly intriguing moment in the
first episode when she's visiting Linda.

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:08.599
When the Doctor encourages Mazikeen to open
up about her guilt after hurting Trixie last

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:12.209
season, the demon is more than a little reluctant
to discuss her emotions.

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:14.219
"So let's talk about what you're dealing with
emotionally.

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:15.760
Yeah, I really don't want to.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.819
Maybe it would help if I spoke your language.

00:04:19.819 --> 00:04:21.360
You speak Lilim?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.729
[speaking in Lilim in a deep voice]
What?"

00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:29.069
In a little shout-out to her birthplace, South
Africa, Lesley-Ann [Brandt] has revealed she

00:04:29.069 --> 00:04:30.229
was speaking Afrikaans.

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:34.289
And if you were wondering what she said, well,
the official Twitter account for Netflix South

00:04:34.289 --> 00:04:36.830
Africa posted her Afrikaans dialogue.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.220
I put that into Google Translate and here's
what it means in English:

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.449
"Can you understand what I'm talking about,
because I want to talk to you and you can't?"

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:49.120
The role of Eve was actually written with
actress Inbar Lavi in mind from the start

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.260
because one of Lucifer's writers was a big
fan of her starring role as a con artist in

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.810
the TV series Imposters.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.690
And what a great choice she was as her decision
to go full-on playing the original sinner

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:03.990
Eve with all the excitement and innocent wonder
of a Disney princess with an extra naughty

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.610
side was absolute genius.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:10.090
And there are lots of lovely little touches
in Eve's scenes from her drink of choice:

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:13.919
an apple martini, to the apples at the bar
and in other scenes.

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:18.470
Then there's her arrival in a heavenly white
dress with a killer pair of fiery heels, to

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:22.060
her later appearances in clothing that's various
shades of red.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:26.400
And there's even some foreshadowing of where
Lucifer and Eve's new relationship is headed

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.430
by the end of the season in the lyrics of
the song playing just before Luci discovers

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.690
she's back on earth.

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:36.720
Also, Eve's conversation with Father Kinley
includes an amusing nod to the opening lines

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.360
of Catholic Confession, "Forgive me, Father,
for I have sinned."

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:39.360
"Forgive me father..

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.270
I am Eve."

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:47.060
Music's always been a big part of the show
and there've been some great musical moments

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.350
this season, kicking off with Lucifer back
at the piano, singing his heart out to Creep;

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:55.009
Maze declaring her love to an oblivious Eve
by singing Wonderwall;

00:05:55.009 --> 00:05:59.639
and Luci, Ella, and Dan getting their groove
on in the season finale with a little throwback

00:05:59.639 --> 00:06:01.080
to Dirty Dancing.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:06.300
Indeed, that toe-tapping season finale could
well pave the way for a full-on musical episode

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:11.410
next season according to co-showrunner Ildy
Modrovich who's been eager to get the cast

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.169
in full song-and-dance mode for some time
now.

00:06:14.169 --> 00:06:18.780
And it looks like actor Tom Ellis would definitely
be up for that because not only is last season's

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:23.099
Luck Be A Lady Tonight scene one of his favourite
moments in the show so far, but he's also

00:06:23.099 --> 00:06:27.410
said that the dance sequence in the finale
was his favourite filming moment of Season

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:28.410
4!

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.530
By the way, we might have never heard Tom
break into song on the show if it hadn't had

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:33.330
been for a cast and crew night out.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:38.030
Originally, the plan for the series was just
for Lucifer to play the piano, but when the

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:42.539
writers heard Tom belt out Mustang Sally at
a karaoke bar, they discovered their lead

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:46.110
actor could really sing and decided to include
it in the show!

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:50.870
Remember the sequence where Amenadiel approaches
random strangers in an effort to connect more

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.520
with human beings now that he's decided to
stay on earth?

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:57.740
Well, when out of the blue he stops by for
a chat with a woman who's working on her laptop

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:03.199
in a coffee shop, the woman he's interrupting
is actually played by one of Lucifer's showrunners,

00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:06.310
Ildy Modrovich, who also wrote this very episode!

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:11.180
And Ildy's co-showrunner, Joe Henderson, snuck
in an easter egg to another one of his creations

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.660
in the scene where Maze and Trixie make up
at the police precinct.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:18.419
Trixie is reading a comic book called "Skyward"
all about the adventures of a young woman

00:07:18.419 --> 00:07:23.449
born into a low-gravity world, and Joe wrote
both the comic book and the episode it appears

00:07:23.449 --> 00:07:24.449
in.

00:07:24.449 --> 00:07:27.900
Trixie's previous reading material in the
show has also provided interesting easter

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.050
eggs, for example, the book "Coraline", that
her mother read to her, was written by Neil

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:37.009
Gaiman the co-creator of The Sandman graphic
novel which introduced the Lucifer character

00:07:37.009 --> 00:07:39.560
that this TV series is loosely based on.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.919
So, were there any other cool details or easter
eggs you spotted in Season 4?

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:46.020
And what were your favourite moments?

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.830
Tap left for my full breakdown of the season
finale plus my season 5 predictions or tap

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:53.110
right for another video you're sure to like.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:56.689
Congratulations to the winner of the last
round of my Avengers giveaway.

00:07:56.689 --> 00:07:59.979
Send me a message from my About page so I
can send you the prize!

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:03.389
And if you enjoyed this, a thumbs-up and a
share are hugely appreciated.

00:08:03.389 --> 00:08:05.780
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:06.840
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

